Being an Announcement for the Edification of Newbies and the Reminding
of Regulars:

The last Saturday of every other month is observed by the gathering of
whatever NetHackish folk can make it at a pub in London for pub food,
good booze, and congenially geekish conversation. July is an other
month on our schedule, so this will be occurring on Saturday 26th,
starting at 14:00 and going on into the early evening (or late
evening, depending), at the regular venue of the Lord Moon of the
Mall, Whitehall.

Directions (slightly tweaked; I wrote them, I get to do that):

The LMotM is at the top of Whitehall; maybe a hundred yards down, on
the right-hand side as you go down from Trafalgar Square. Nearest tube
Charing Cross, though Westminster isn't that much further away for
those for whom that's quicker to get to. Look for people who are
either outright wearing NetHack T-shirts, or just looking generally
geek-like.

